<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#tulughma">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tulughma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tulughma was a flanking tactic of Central Asian origin in which mobile cavalry units swept around the enemy's flanks to attack them from the sides and rear. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> used it at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-panipat">First Battle of Panipat</a> in 1526. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> profile records that the sultanate's army of approximately 100,000 was destroyed there by Babur's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">field artillery</a> combined with flanking tulughma tactics.</p></div>
